Ruckig generates trajectories from a current position, velocity and acceleration
to a target state. It applies velocity, acceleration and jerk limits to each
degree of freedom and synchronizes the result across multiple axes.

This package installs the C++20 shared library, headers and CMake package export.
The cloud client, Python bindings, examples and benchmark are disabled. The
library preserves upstream's unversioned ABI. Tests use simulated trajectories;
they do not establish physical actuator safety or control-loop deadlines.
